{"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CartesianProductView"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CartesianProductView","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView.swift#L48","fileName":"CartesianProductView.swift"},"title":"CartesianProductView","externalID":"s:13GraphProducts20CartesianProductViewV","modules":[{"name":"GraphProducts"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Cartesian product G □ H of two graphs, both directed or both undirected, as a lazy view."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Made by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cartesianProductView(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView\/EdgeIndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView\/UndirectedEdges"],"anchor":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView\/first","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/CartesianProductView\/second"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"generated":true,"title":"Enumerations","identifiers":["doc:\/\